##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.1
##Scene A plane rippled by its material's displacement, lit from the side
version 3.03
Format 64 48 1
PixelSamples 8 8
Projection "orthographic"
Clipping 1 100
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 0 "intensity" [0.1]
# from the left, so a ripple's near slope is lit and its far slope is in shade
LightSource "distantlight" 1 "intensity" [1] "to" [0.8 0 1]
# three ripples across x, moving the plane up to 0.16 toward the camera. The plane's normal
# points away from the camera, so the material's lift is negative. A subdivision surface of one
# face whose boundary is interpolated is the flat quad, and is the shape the new core displaces
Attribute "displacementbound" "float sphere" [0.16]
Bxdf "materialx" "rippled" "string file" ["data/rippled.mtlx"] "string material" ["rippled"]
SubdivisionMesh "catmull-clark" [4] [0 1 2 3] ["interpolateboundary"] [0 0] [] []
    "P" [-1.2 -0.9 5  1.2 -0.9 5  1.2 0.9 5  -1.2 0.9 5]
WorldEnd
